  "Solution": {
    "S": "We have $x^2 - x - 2 = (x-2)(x+1)$. The expression is negative between $-1$ and $2$, and positive outside.\n\nThus:\n\n$$\\int_{-2}^{2} |x^2 - x - 2| \\, dx = \\int_{-2}^{-1} (x^2 - x - 2) \\, dx + \\int_{-1}^{2} -(x^2 - x - 2) \\, dx$$\n\n$$= \\int_{-2}^{-1} (x^2 - x - 2) \\, dx + \\int_{-1}^{2} (-x^2 + x + 2) \\, dx$$\n\n$$= \\left[ \\frac{x^3}{3} - \\frac{x^2}{2} - 2x \\right]_{-2}^{-1} + \\left[ -\\frac{x^3}{3} + \\frac{x^2}{2} + 2x \\right]_{-1}^{2}$$\n\nEvaluating:\n\nAt $x = -1$: $-\\frac{1}{3} - \\frac{1}{2} + 2 = \\frac{-2 - 3 + 12}{6} = \\frac{7}{6}$\n\nAt $x = -2$: $-\\frac{8}{3} - 2 + 4 = \\frac{-8 - 6 + 12}{3} = -\\frac{2}{3}$\n\nFirst part = $\\frac{7}{6} - \\left(-\\frac{2}{3}\\right) = \\frac{7}{6} + \\frac{4}{6} = \\frac{11}{6}$\n\nSecond part:\n\nAt $x = 2$: $-\\frac{8}{3} + 2 + 4 = \\frac{-8 + 6 + 12}{3} = \\frac{10}{3}$\n\nAt $x = -1$: $\\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{2} - 2 = \\frac{2 + 3 - 12}{6} = -\\frac{7}{6}$\n\nSecond part = $\\frac{10}{3} - \\left(-\\frac{7}{6}\\right) = \\frac{20}{6} + \\frac{7}{6} = \\frac{27}{6} = \\frac{9}{2}$\n\nTotal = $\\frac{11}{6} + \\frac{27}{6} = \\frac{38}{6} = \\frac{19}{3}$\n\nThus the correct option is B: $\\frac{19}{3}$."
  },
